JavaScript code:
```
// Set the date of the winter holidays
var winterHolidaysDate = new Date("December 25, 2021 00:00:00").getTime();
// Update the countdown every second
var x = setInterval(function() {
  // Get the current date and time
  var now = new Date().getTime();
  // Calculate the time remaining until the winter holidays
  var distance = winterHolidaysDate - now;
  // Calculate the days, hours, minutes, and seconds remaining
  var days = Math.floor(distance / (1000 * 60 * 60 * 24));
  var hours = Math.floor((distance % (1000 * 60 * 60 * 24)) / (1000 * 60 * 60));
  var minutes = Math.floor((distance % (1000 * 60 * 60)) / (1000 * 60));
  var seconds = Math.floor((distance % (1000 * 60)) / 1000);
  // Display the countdown timer
  document.getElementById("countdown").innerHTML = days + "d " + hours + "h "
  + minutes + "m " + seconds + "s ";
  // Display a message when the winter holidays arrive
  if (distance < 0) {
    clearInterval(x);
    document.getElementById("countdown").innerHTML = "Winter holidays have arrived!";
  }
}, 1000);
```
This code will display a message "Winter holidays are coming!" and a countdown timer on your website. The timer will update every second and display the days, hours, minutes, and seconds remaining until the winter holidays. When the winter holidays arrive, the message will change to "Winter holidays have arrived!". You can customize the message and date to fit your needs.

