Here's a sample Java code that can generate an opening for a news article based on a given headline:
```java
public class NewsArticle {

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String headline = "Scientists discover new species of bird in Amazon rainforest";
        String[] keywords = {"Scientists", "new species", "bird", "Amazon rainforest"};
        String[] sentences = {"In a groundbreaking discovery, scientists have found a new species of bird in the Amazon rainforest.",
                              "The bird, which has not been previously documented, is a significant find for the scientific community.",
                              "According to the researchers, the bird has distinctive features that set it apart from other species in the region.",
                              "The discovery was made after years of research and exploration in the Amazon rainforest.",
                              "This new species of bird is expected to provide valuable insights into the biodiversity of the region."};
        String opening = generateOpening(headline, keywords, sentences);
        System.out.println(opening);
    }

    public static String generateOpening(String headline, String[] keywords, String[] sentences) {
        String opening = "";
        String[] headlineWords = headline.split("\\s+");
        for (String word : headlineWords) {
            if (containsKeyword(word, keywords)) {
                opening += word + " ";
            }
        }
        opening = opening.trim() + ". ";
        opening += sentences[(int) (Math.random() * sentences.length)];
        return opening;
    }

    public static boolean containsKeyword(String word, String[] keywords) {
        for (String keyword : keywords) {
            if (word.toLowerCase().contains(keyword.toLowerCase())) {
                return true;
            }
        }
        return false;
    }
}
```
In this code, the `generateOpening` method takes in the headline, an array of keywords, and an array of sentences. It first searches for the keywords in the headline and adds them to the opening. Then, it randomly selects one of the sentences to complete the opening.
You can customize the `keywords` and `sentences` arrays to fit the specific news article you are generating an opening for.

